1. DEFINITIONS

"ArabianCurb Additions" means the Arabic-mode reference files, ArabianCurb
branding and assets, Arabic-specific documentation, installer modifications,
and other original modifications authored for this repository by Loay
Abdalslam. It does not include the upstream VibeCurb materials identified in
Section 8.

"Tool" means the ArabianCurb Additions, whether used alone or together with
the upstream VibeCurb materials, including any substantial copy, modification,
adaptation, or derivative of the ArabianCurb Additions.

"Website" means a website, web application, landing page, digital experience,
or substantially similar web deliverable whose design, code, imagery, motion,
branding, or other material output was created or materially assisted by the
Tool.

"Website Sale" means any future sale, assignment, transfer, or other disposal
of ownership of a Website for monetary or non-monetary consideration.

"Gross Website Sale Price" means the total consideration agreed for the
Website Sale before deducting commissions, development costs, platform fees,
expenses, or similar charges. If a Website is sold as part of a larger bundled
transaction and no separate Website price is stated, the licensee must make a
reasonable, good-faith allocation of the transaction price to the Website.

2. LICENSE GRANT

Subject to every condition in this license, Loay Abdalslam grants you a
non-exclusive, worldwide license to use, copy, modify, and distribute the
ArabianCurb Additions for personal, educational, internal, and commercial
work.

3. COMMERCIAL WEBSITE SALE ROYALTY

If you use the Tool to create or materially assist a Website and that Website
is sold at any time in the future, you agree to pay Loay Abdalslam a royalty
equal to ten percent (10%) of the Gross Website Sale Price.

This royalty applies:

- regardless of the original or final Website Sale price;
- regardless of when the Website Sale occurs;
- whether the Tool was used directly or through a modified or derivative
  workflow; and
- whether or not the ArabianCurb Additions remain visible in the final
  Website.

The royalty becomes due within thirty (30) calendar days after the licensee
receives any part of the Website Sale consideration. If the consideration is
paid in installments, ten percent (10%) of each installment becomes due
within thirty (30) calendar days after that installment is received.

4. PROFESSIONAL HONOR SYSTEM

This royalty condition is administered solely through professional honesty,
good faith, and the licensee's voluntary self-reporting. ArabianCurb does not
include telemetry for this purpose, and this license does not grant Loay
Abdalslam a routine right to inspect or audit the licensee's private books,
systems, client records, or source code.

The honor-based administration of the royalty does not change the agreed
royalty amount or payment timing in Section 3.

